WEBVTT

00:00:03.330 --> 00:00:07.530
<v Sarah Okafor>Morning, everyone. Monday the twenty-second of June. Have we got everyone on?</v>

00:00:09.890 --> 00:00:16.190
<v Fiona Doyle>Yeah, I'm here. Still mourning the broken coffee machine in the canteen, though. That was a disappointing start.</v>

00:00:18.469 --> 00:00:23.019
<v Marcus Hale>You say disappointing. I'd say the coffee was fairly disappointing when it worked.</v>

00:00:23.719 --> 00:00:28.969
<v Priya Raman>Morning. Sorry, came in over the end of that. My headset's doing its own thing.</v>

00:00:30.250 --> 00:00:38.299
<v Sarah Okafor>Only coffee complaints. And the charity bake sale on Friday got a better reception than the coffee ever has. Anyway, enough cake chat.</v>

00:00:39.310 --> 00:00:42.109
<v Tomasz Nowak>That's the shortest cake discussion we've ever had.</v>

00:00:43.259 --> 00:00:46.409
<v Sarah Okafor>Right, closed stuff first, then what actually needs doing.</v>

00:00:47.049 --> 00:00:54.049
<v Fiona Doyle>I finished the repair on the number two bearing last night. That's done, not something to carry into today's list.</v>

00:00:55.869 --> 00:00:57.070
<v Sarah Okafor>Good, closed. Thanks.</v>

00:00:58.350 --> 00:01:05.349
<v Hannah Price>Same sort of update from me: finished the repair on the line two last night. Nothing outstanding on that repair.</v>

00:01:06.209 --> 00:01:09.359
<v Marcus Hale>Lovely. Two things off rather than another six on.</v>

00:01:09.890 --> 00:01:17.939
<v Tomasz Nowak>Just an observation from nights: noticed the dryer was running a bit warm, but it settled down. Not raising a job from that.</v>

00:01:19.569 --> 00:01:24.469
<v Olumide Adeyemi>Yeah, understood. Settled back down, so that's history rather than a new temperature job.</v>

00:01:26.319 --> 00:01:32.969
<v Hannah Price>And I heard a slight rattle from the line 1. Nothing to action yet, just mentioning what I heard.</v>

00:01:33.599 --> 00:01:37.799
<v Sarah Okafor>Noted as an observation only. Neither of those is an extra action.</v>

00:01:38.840 --> 00:01:45.489
<v Sarah Okafor>On the blocked side, we can't get to the Boiler Safety Relief Valve until production gives us a window.</v>

00:01:46.920 --> 00:01:53.569
<v Olumide Adeyemi>And we're still waiting on parts for the Boiler Safety Relief Valve. Nothing we can do until they arrive.</v>

00:01:54.150 --> 00:01:58.000
<v Priya Raman>So it's both access and parts, not just one of them.</v>

00:01:58.530 --> 00:02:02.379
<v Sarah Okafor>Exactly. Still blocked, no new action against it in this meeting.</v>

00:02:03.150 --> 00:02:11.550
<v Sarah Okafor>Olu, can you chase the purchase order for the waste heat boiler, tomorrow at 9:30? It's not an emergency but don't let it slip.</v>

00:02:12.530 --> 00:02:16.729
<v Olumide Adeyemi>The purchase order itself, yeah? Not chasing a delivery date as well?</v>

00:02:19.090 --> 00:02:24.340
<v Sarah Okafor>Yeah, just chase the purchase order for the waste heat boiler. Keep it to that.</v>

00:02:25.300 --> 00:02:30.900
<v Olumide Adeyemi>Okay, I'll chase that tomorrow at 9:30. Not an emergency, but I won't let it slip.</v>

00:02:32.819 --> 00:02:35.969
<v Fiona Doyle>Got it. Separate from the valve parts discussion, then.</v>

00:02:36.370 --> 00:02:43.719
<v Sarah Okafor>Fiona Doyle, could you book a contractor to look at the Stretch Wrapper by 11am, if you've got a spare minute?</v>

00:02:45.990 --> 00:02:50.189
<v Fiona Doyle>Yeah. Just checking—booking made by 11am, not somebody physically here by eleven?</v>

00:02:51.620 --> 00:02:56.520
<v Sarah Okafor>That's right, the booking by 11am. We're not agreeing a contractor visit time here.</v>

00:02:59.000 --> 00:03:05.300
<v Fiona Doyle>Fine, I'll book a contractor to look at the Stretch Wrapper by 11am. I can fit that in.</v>

00:03:07.610 --> 00:03:11.110
<v Marcus Hale>A spare minute. Rare bit of kit, one of those.</v>

00:03:11.469 --> 00:03:18.469
<v Sarah Okafor>Yeah, well. The seals on the line one HPU also need replacing today, normal priority. Anyone able to take that?</v>

00:03:18.919 --> 00:03:23.120
<v Tomasz Nowak>Um, I can't take that on. Don't put my name against it.</v>

00:03:25.289 --> 00:03:28.439
<v Priya Raman>No capacity from me for the seals either, sorry.</v>

00:03:30.449 --> 00:03:38.500
<v Sarah Okafor>Right, replacing the seals on the line one HPU stays unassigned. Still needed today at normal priority, but we've not got an owner.</v>

00:03:39.889 --> 00:03:45.490
<v Hannah Price>I'll update the risk assessment for work on the CV01. I'll drop everything for that one.</v>

00:03:47.550 --> 00:03:50.349
<v Sarah Okafor>Thanks, Han. Agreed, that takes precedence for you.</v>

00:03:52.719 --> 00:03:59.719
<v Hannah Price>Yeah, the risk assessment update, to be clear. I'm not saying the work on the CV01 itself is signed off.</v>

00:04:00.099 --> 00:04:03.250
<v Olumide Adeyemi>Yep, understood. The document, not permission to crack on.</v>

00:04:05.099 --> 00:04:10.349
<v Sarah Okafor>And I'll clear the jam and check the sensors on the Palletiser today at 2pm.</v>

00:04:11.449 --> 00:04:16.699
<v Marcus Hale>Sorry, Sarah, you were breaking up. You're taking both bits, the jam and the sensors?</v>

00:04:18.300 --> 00:04:23.899
<v Sarah Okafor>Both, yeah. I'll clear the jam and check the sensors on the Palletiser, today at 2pm.</v>

00:04:25.990 --> 00:04:29.139
<v Priya Raman>Under isolation for access, obviously. Not a reach-in-and-wiggle-it situation.</v>

00:04:29.889 --> 00:04:32.689
<v Sarah Okafor>Absolutely, under the proper isolation procedure. No shortcuts.</v>

00:04:34.300 --> 00:04:43.750
<v Olumide Adeyemi>There's also recalibrating the sensors on the dryer. That needs doing this afternoon. Not an emergency but don't let it slip. I can't take it, though—anyone else?</v>

00:04:45.009 --> 00:04:51.660
<v Tomasz Nowak>I can't cover that either. And just to separate it out, my warm-running comment wasn't a request for recalibration.</v>

00:04:52.769 --> 00:04:58.019
<v Olumide Adeyemi>Yeah, separate item. The recalibration still needs doing, but no one's offered to own it.</v>

00:05:00.259 --> 00:05:08.660
<v Sarah Okafor>Okay, recalibrate the sensors on the dryer: this afternoon, not an emergency but don't let it slip. Unassigned, not an agreed commitment from anyone.</v>

00:05:09.310 --> 00:05:16.660
<v Fiona Doyle>I'll do the lock-out tag-out sign-off on the HV board on Monday. That's holding production up so it needs doing first.</v>

00:05:18.279 --> 00:05:21.779
<v Priya Raman>Just the sign-off you're taking, not the HV switching itself?</v>

00:05:22.990 --> 00:05:28.589
<v Fiona Doyle>Correct, I'll do the lock-out tag-out sign-off on the HV board. I'm not taking on switching.</v>

00:05:29.459 --> 00:05:34.360
<v Sarah Okafor>Thanks, Fiona Doyle. Monday is today, so that's clear, and the sign-off is yours.</v>

00:05:36.529 --> 00:05:40.379
<v Fiona Doyle>Yep. That comes first for me because it's holding production up.</v>

00:05:41.800 --> 00:05:48.449
<v Sarah Okafor>Han, can you check the guarding on the IM2 by Wednesday? Not an emergency but don't let it slip.</v>

00:05:49.829 --> 00:05:56.829
<v Hannah Price>Yeah, I'll check the guarding on the IM2 by Wednesday. Not an emergency, understood, but I won't let it drift.</v>

00:05:58.790 --> 00:06:03.339
<v Sarah Okafor>And that doesn't displace the CV01 risk assessment. That's still your drop-everything one.</v>

00:06:04.529 --> 00:06:09.079
<v Hannah Price>Exactly. CV01 risk assessment takes precedence; IM2 guarding check by Wednesday. Both clear.</v>

00:06:09.959 --> 00:06:13.110
<v Fiona Doyle>That's a fairly full page for a Monday morning.</v>

00:06:13.420 --> 00:06:16.920
<v Tomasz Nowak>And Teams only swallowed about half a sentence. We're improving.</v>

00:06:18.550 --> 00:06:21.699
<v Olumide Adeyemi>Don't praise it. That's when it drops the call.</v>

00:06:22.110 --> 00:06:26.660
<v Sarah Okafor>Any corrections to what we've agreed? Just corrections, rather than opening another list.</v>

00:06:27.459 --> 00:06:28.860
<v Priya Raman>No corrections from me.</v>

00:06:30.750 --> 00:06:32.149
<v Marcus Hale>No, all clear here.</v>

00:06:32.730 --> 00:06:35.180
<v Sarah Okafor>Right, thanks everyone. We'll leave it there.</v>
